# Dice of Dionysus — Cursor Rules

Vanilla JS, class-based roguelike dice game (Balatro-inspired). `GameEngine.state` is the single run state. End goal: playable desktop `.exe` via Tauri (`npm run tauri:build`), alongside the web/PWA build.

Philosophy: stable shipping, small diffs, no framework churn. Enforcement lives in tests, not prose — if a rule matters, it should be a failing test in `tests/unit/`, not a paragraph in a doc nobody re-reads.

## Critical habits

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Use run `prng` (`SeededRNG`) for gameplay randomness | `Math.random()` for rolls, shop pools, scoring |
| Add cards in `game/js/data/gameData.js` first | Scatter card definitions elsewhere |
| Pass dependencies explicitly (`game`, `gameEngine`) when adding new call sites | Add new `window.game`/`window.uiManager`/etc. reach-throughs |
| Use `Logger` in game code | Rely on `console.log` |
| Boons = equipped; consumables = Libations/Worship (see `docs/GAME_TERMINOLOGY.md`) | Confuse naming with unrelated terms |
| Run `npm test` before calling a change done | Assume a change works because it "should" |

## Guardrails (enforced, not just documented)

`tests/unit/architecture-guardrails.test.js` ratchets file size and global-coupling counts for the known god-object files (`GameEngine.js`, `Boon.js`, `ShopUI.js`, `BalatroEffects.js`, `boonTimingHandlers.js`, `Main.js`). It fails `npm test` if any of them grow past their current baseline. If you need to add real functionality to one of these files, extract something out first so the file doesn't cross its ceiling — don't raise the ceiling to make room.

## Verify

`npm run dev` (port 3000) · `npm run lint:fix` · `npm run test` · `npm run playtest:boons` when boon/scoring flow changes.

## Map

- Engine/logic: `game/js/engine/` (ScoringEngine, HandEvaluator, ShopStockGenerator — keep DOM-free)
- Game state + orchestration: `game/js/game/GameEngine.js`
- Cards/data: `game/js/classes/`, `game/js/data/gameData.js`
- UI: `game/js/ui/`, `game/js/ui/renderers/`
- Desktop packaging: `src-tauri/`
